  "configuration_id": "config_046",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_043 (scvi_n200, vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250 acc. All top-4 results cluster in a narrow 0.713–0.725 band, and the only major untested variable in the best architecture is the RNA encoder type. scgpt was catastrophic (0.52), but pca_n2000 has never been tested in any multimodal setting. Question: Can a simpler linear RNA encoder (pca_n2000) match or exceed scvi_n200 when paired with the best-known aggregation (transformer) and fusion (weighted)? This is critical because if pca_n2000 performs comparably, it is substantially cheaper (no learned RNA model to train), freeing GPU budget for further refinement in the remaining 3 experiments. If it underperforms, we confirm scvi_n200 is the right encoder and can exploit that direction. Rationale: With only 3 experiments left, resolving this uncertainty about the single largest untested architectural choice is the highest-information experiment. Expected cost: ~2.5–3.2 GPU hours (PCA encoding is negligible compared to scvi; the dominant cost is the ViT-L image encoder and transformer fusion, similar to config_043's 3.60 h but without the scvi pre-training overhead), making it a cost-effective probe."
}

